{% extends 'owner/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Menu Scanner — Data &amp; Privacy Policy — S2S{% endblock %}
{% block page_title %}Scanner Privacy Policy{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<style>
.scanner-privacy {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 0 60px;
}
.scanner-privacy-hero {
    background: #18120a;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 36px 32px;
    margin-bottom: 36px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 20px;
}
.scanner-privacy-hero-icon {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(232, 160, 32, .12);
    border: 1.5px solid rgba(232, 160, 32, .3);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
}
.scanner-privacy-hero h1 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #E8A020;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
}
.scanner-privacy-hero p {
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: .875rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, .5);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
}
.scanner-privacy-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 5px;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: .68rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: #E8A020;
    color: #18120a;
    padding: 3px 8px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.scanner-privacy-notice {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    background: #fff8ed;
    border: 1.5px solid #fce8b2;
    border-radius: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: .875rem;
    color: #6b5033;
    line-height: 1.6;
}
.scanner-privacy-section {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #ede4d6;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 24px 26px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
}
.scanner-privacy-section h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #18120a;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
}
.scanner-privacy-section h2 span { font-size: 1.15rem; }
.scanner-privacy-section p,
.scanner-privacy-section li {
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: .875rem;
    color: #5c4a35;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
}
.scanner-privacy-section ul {
    margin: 8px 0 0 18px;
    padding: 0;
}
.scanner-privacy-section li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
.scanner-privacy-empty-banner {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f9f7f4 0%, #faf2e6 100%);
    border: 2px dashed #e3c97a;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 28px 24px;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 24px;
}
.scanner-privacy-empty-banner p {
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: .9rem;
    color: #9c8052;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
}
.scanner-privacy-empty-banner strong {
    display: block;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: #7a5c1a;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
}
</style>

<div class="scanner-privacy">

    {# ── Hero ── #}
    <div class="scanner-privacy-hero">
        <div class="scanner-privacy-hero-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E8A020" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
            </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
            <div class="scanner-privacy-badge">Beta feature</div>
            <h1>Menu Scanner — Data &amp; Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p>This policy covers how Scan to See collects and uses data from the Menu Scanner beta feature.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    {# Data terms notice #}
    <div class="scanner-privacy-notice">
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#E8A020" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" style="flex-shrink:0;margin-top:1px"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
        <span>The scanner is optional. You must accept these data terms before every scanning session, and you can build the same menu manually without uploading an image.</span>
    </div>

    {# ── Sections ── #}
    <div class="scanner-privacy-section">
        <h2><span class="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">photo_camera</span> What data we collect</h2>
        <p>When you use the Menu Scanner, we may collect the following types of data:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>The menu image you upload (the photograph of your physical menu).</li>
            <li>The extracted items, categories, prices, and quality metrics produced by the AI pipeline.</li>
            <li>Metadata such as scan time, the associated account, business and menu while the account exists, model information, and the currency setting.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="scanner-privacy-section">
        <h2><span class="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">target</span> How we use this data</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>To process your scan and return structured menu results to you.</li>
            <li>To improve the accuracy and performance of the AI recognition model.</li>
            <li>To monitor scan quality and diagnose pipeline errors.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do <strong>not</strong> use your data for advertising, and we do <strong>not</strong> sell it to any third party.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="scanner-privacy-section">
        <h2><span class="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">lock</span> Storage and safeguards</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Scan images are stored in configured Cloudinary object storage and scan records are stored in the application database.</li>
            <li>Images are not made public as menu pages merely because they were scanned. Access is limited to operational and dataset-development purposes.</li>
            <li>Failed scans and scans with no useful detected regions are removed from training storage.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="scanner-privacy-section">
        <h2><span class="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">schedule</span> Data retention</h2>
        <p>When you delete the account, failed, incomplete, and unreviewed scan records and their stored training images are removed. A scan that you reviewed and corrected may remain for model evaluation and training after its links to your account, email, business, and menu records are removed.</p>
        <p>Because source-menu content may identify a business, retained records are treated as de-linked or pseudonymized data and are not promised to be anonymous. They are retained only while useful for the beta dataset and should be periodically reviewed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="scanner-privacy-section">
        <h2><span class="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">front_hand</span> Your choices and rights</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>You have the right to access the data we hold about your scans.</li>
            <li>You have the right to request correction or deletion of your scan data.</li>
            <li>You can stop creating new scanner data at any time by using the manual menu editor.</li>
            <li>Depending on applicable law, additional access, objection, restriction, portability, or deletion rights may apply.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="scanner-privacy-empty-banner">
        <strong>Read the complete policy</strong>
        <p>These scanner-specific terms supplement the <a href="{{ path('app_privacy') }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">S2S Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="{{ path('app_terms') }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Terms of Service</a>. The beta documents require qualified legal review before commercial production.</p>
    </div>

</div>
{% endblock %}
